    <DataNode elementId="AT4G30440-MONOMER" textLabel="UDP-glucuronate 4-epimerase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT4G30440-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; gene &lt;i&gt;GAE1&lt;/i&gt; was heterologously expressed in the yeast &lt;i&gt;Pichia pastoris&lt;/i&gt;. Crude extracts of the recombinant yeast were shown to catalyze the 4-epimerization of UDP-glucuronate and UDP-galacturonate |CITS: [15247385]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G30440-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-122" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT4G30440.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT4G30440" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightExp" value="50." />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightKd" value="50." />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_15247385" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT1G02000-MONOMER" textLabel="AT1G02000-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT1G02000-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The enzyme encoded by &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis GAE2&lt;/i&gt; is similar to that encoded by &lt;i&gt;GAE1&lt;/i&gt;, which has been shown to have UDP-glucuronate 4-epimerase activity |CITS:[15247385]|. Although it has been postulated that GAE2 also has this activity, this assessment has not been experimentally verified.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G02000-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-129" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT1G02000.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT1G02000" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_15247385" />
